{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/439651-how-crazy-are-your-changelings","id":439651,"title":"How crazy are your changelings?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-13T02:47:17-07:00","id":439651,"title":"How crazy are your changelings?","content":"So this is another basic question about how you all see the world of the Lost.<br /> <br /> In part it is kind of a basic question about what number of Clarity your NPC:s and PC:s usually end up with.<br /> Are there some amount of Clarity that you feel changelings usually ends up with? A stable amount perhaps where they are able to have a decent existence without suffering breaking points?<br /> <br /> In my chronicle (although that was admittedly too fast-paced for this game) neither the PC:s nor their allies could ever hold onto a Clarity above six due to seven having the breaking point of &quot;major life change&quot; which constitutes one or more moment in pretty much every scenario.<br /> <br /> The second part of the question concerns how crazy your changeling characters seems. If anyone could give actual examples of how changelings in there chronicles have acted while having different levels of Clarity I\u00b4d be really interested in reading about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4908-dreaming-johnny","name":"Dreaming Johnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T08:39:48-07:00","id":439965,"title":"","content":"I am rather lenient with the life altering situation in regards to scenarios. I don't tend to include stuff the PCs have been working towards for some time, and the alteration must be rather permanent. Having said so, Clarity 7 is a bit of a challenge to hold to. The PCs don't have all too many Resources, so petty theft is pretty common and sometimes they do pick rather extreme sollutions to a problem (e.g. we need more information: lets kidnap the cultist). Still, they do keep an eye on their Clarity, and nobody has of yet dropped below 6. As for NPCs, those with an active hand in the mortal world are likely to have a Clarity of 5 to 7 (average 6). Those who stick to the Hedge and are more involved with Changelings, Fae and goblins can get lower (3 to 5).<br /> <br /> In regards to acting, it has actually not come up that often since my PCs have not yet interacted intensely with low Clarity changelings at all except for one. They certainly realized that particular NPC had trouble with interacting with the mortal world. I had her react to mortals and events in a way that made sense to her personality and background amongst the fey, but not to what really happened. For example, she was really scared of cars, treating them as growling angry monsters and had trouble keeping her calm when questioned by the lawyer of the PCs since she kept seeing flashes of him as a Fae (which he was not) offering her some deal. She has a Clarity of 2 btw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T12:31:39-07:00","id":440298,"title":"","content":"Normally mine hover at about 5/6 depending on how long the game went. There was one exception to this, but it was by design- the character was a fairest bright one/moonborn with a lot of dots in contracts of the moon, lucidity and severance. AND he was an autumn courtier, because if I'm going to play a pretty lunatic, he might as well be a scary pretty lunatic.<br /> <br /> We played for two years. That I got him through six months is still one of my proudest achievements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/768-djehuty3","name":"djehuty3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T18:30:18-07:00","id":440744,"title":"","content":"At nearly a year old, <i>Malibu Dream House</i> has 3 characters at 7 (Gawain, Lorelei, Insincere Marguerite) one at 6 (Ace) and two at 5 (Calamity and Jacob). I can't right off recall the Clarities of the folks in my old <i>Beyond the Sea </i>game, but I think it was mostly in the 7-5 range also.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T00:02:08-07:00","id":441038,"title":"","content":"Me beloved Summer King, Lionheart, was floating around Clarity 2 or 3. You don't torture your boyfriend to death and launch a violent coup with high morality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T09:39:55-07:00","id":441503,"title":"","content":"My guy ended up with 5, and was pondering having a break to 4 by breaking a pledge. I think after that point there wasn't much he was likely to do, since he wasn't a fan of violence and was also spectacularly bad at it. Our leader was at 4, the others probably around 6 or maybe even 7. Anise was trying to become a True Fae so probably would have dropped lower than 4 if we kept it up and likely counts as crazy for most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T05:06:22-07:00","id":442427,"title":"","content":"Okay, so what sort of symptoms do your different changelings manifest at the different levels? Is it just hallucinations from the Hedge or do you suffer from other things? Do you make changelings develop strange quirks even while on Clarity 7? Sort of like the boons and banes that appear at very high levels of Wyrd.<br /> <br /> I tried to have both my PC:s and NPC:s being at risk from their visions, a &quot;seeings is believing&quot; kind of thing. Like a bike could kick and damage a changeling who thought it was a lively steed. Or adding several flights of stairs to a church tower for the changelings with the lowest Clarity.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think about these sort of things? Do they fit with the fiction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4908-dreaming-johnny","name":"Dreaming Johnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T12:25:48-07:00","id":442944,"title":"","content":"I haven't really done anything at 7. Since 5 is where they lose Kenning and start getting penalties, I tend to start there. I do something throw in odd things when describing the scene for lower Clarity Changelings. It's more subtle at 5 than it is for someone who slips lower, but there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T12:54:43-07:00","id":443004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaming Johnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/439651-how-crazy-are-your-changelings?p=442427#post442427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried to have both my PC:s and NPC:s being at risk from their visions, a &quot;seeings is believing&quot; kind of thing. Like a bike could kick and damage a changeling who thought it was a lively steed. Or adding several flights of stairs to a church tower for the changelings with the lowest Clarity.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think about these sort of things? Do they fit with the fiction?</div> </div> </div> </div>That should be fine. Some of it should probably be in the players hands, mixing the rules of worlds occasionally.<br /> <br /> My ST used it to give hints of their Keeper's Hunt for them, in addition to general hallucinations and visions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T18:16:06-07:00","id":443459,"title":"","content":"I've followed the same general lines as the Baron: throwing in subtle descriptive things at 5 and below. One trick I tried was throwing in random details into a description then denying that I did.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, you're walking through the market. You see various stalls, crowds of local changelings, your Keeper, hobgoblins selling their wares...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What?! My Keeper is here?! I run away!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay... From what?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;My Keeper!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Um... Your Keeper isn't there.&quot;<br /> <br /> They got what I was trying to do and ran with it. The ST should try things like that out, allowing the behavioural aspects of the character's low Clarity to be acted out by the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T08:56:47-07:00","id":444329,"title":"","content":"in the games that i run, all changelings (regardless of Clarity rating) are &quot;crazy&quot; in relation to the majority of the non-altered humans around them. Sanity stopped being an option for them when they were forced to survive in Arcadia. Clarity represents how cognizant they are of their condition, the higher the rating the more aware they are of their own delusions and as such have a better ways of coping with their collection of derangements and manias.<br /> <br /> As their Clarity drops, the less control they have their own psychoses and the more they become what they were in the Fairest of Lands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","user":"Firefly Night","date":". 03-28-2015, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T18:19:19-07:00","id":449968,"title":"","content":"When asking that question, you have to consider all the freaky crap Changelings have to deal with on a regular basis. If not the Hedge and the denizens therein, they at least meet with each other frequently enough. Also take into account they feed on people's emotions and have the power to influence their dreams. Not exactly beings who are going to remain sane for very long unless they've attained a level of Zen-like mellowness.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, I'd like to imagine going the Requiem style of things, in which you typical Changeling balances out around 4 or 5, while only the careless go lower and the rebellious go higher. As for symptoms, I'd like to imagine that creatures from a realm that thrives on imagination is much more primal than Earth's. When a Changeling of low Clarity has an episode, I like to imagine them being caught in some sort of manic fit, their emotions and personalities fluctuating to the extreme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-19-2015, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}